      "id": "AF-ACM-002",
      "question": "Explain how to perform a ring (coin tap) test and how is a defect detected?",
      "idealAnswer": "A ring (coin tap) test is performed by lightly taping the suspect area to be inspected with a round coin like object or a special tap test hammer that is designed specifically for a tap test. Listen for a solid clear sharp ring response or a dull thud sound. If while performing the test you hear a dull thud sound, this area is suspect of delamination and must be inspected further.",
